+# OpenAlgo Upgrade-Proof Plan for the POV Engine
+
+> Status: PLAN ONLY (no code changed yet)
+> Date: 2025-12-19
+> Author: Institutional algo-desk analysis
+
+---
+
+## 1. Current state audit (what I found in your repo)
+
+### ✅ Already upgrade-safe
+| Item | Why it's safe |
+|---|---|
+| `pov_engine/` (entire folder) | Self-contained package. Only talks to OpenAlgo via the **public SDK** (`from openalgo import api` + REST/WS). Zero imports from `blueprints/`, `database/`, `broker/`, `restx_api/`, etc. |
+| `pov_engine/core/client.py` | Connects purely via `OPENALGO_API_KEY` / `HOST_SERVER` / `WEBSOCKET_URL` env vars. Survives any UI/backend rewrite. |
+| `pov_engine/input/*.json` | Pure data — untouched by upgrades. |
+| `pov_engine/_sdkpath.py` | Shields the engine from the local empty `openalgo/openalgo/` package collision. |
+
+### ⚠️ At risk (coupling points an upgrade WILL touch)
+| # | File | Coupling | Upgrade risk |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | `app.py` (lines 87, 343) | imports + registers `blueprints/pov_terminal.py` | **HIGH** — `git pull` overwrites `app.py`; your import line vanishes (non-fatal only if the blueprint file also disappears) |
+| 2 | `blueprints/pov_terminal.py` | your custom file inside upstream dir | **HIGH** — untracked but adjacent; an installer/fresh-clone loses it |
+| 3 | `run_pov.py` (repo root) | launcher, untracked | **MEDIUM** — survives `git pull`, lost on `git clean -fd` / fresh clone |
+| 4 | `docker-compose.yaml` — `pov-dash` service (lines 53–90) | custom service added to upstream compose | **HIGH** — upstream compose is tracked; pull causes conflict or silent overwrite |
+| 5 | Historical evidence | `strategies/Custom Statergy/POV/` (older engine) shows **deleted** in your git status | Proof an upgrade already wiped a POV folder once |
+
+### Verdict
+> **Yes — your POV engine can be made 100% upgrade-proof.** The engine itself already is.
+> What needs hardening is the *wiring* (blueprint, compose service, launcher), which today
+> lives inside OpenAlgo's tracked files.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Target architecture (master project directory)
+
+```
+my-trading-system/                  <-- master project dir
+│
+├── docker-compose.yml              <-- launches BOTH apps with one click
+├── .env                            <-- shared secrets (OPENALGO_API_KEY, ports)
+│
+├── openalgo/                       <-- PRISTINE upstream clone — DO NOT TOUCH
+│   ├── app.py, templates/, blueprints/ ...
+│   └── Dockerfile
+│
+├── pov_engine/                     <-- YOUR code — 100% upgrade-proof
+│   ├── Dockerfile                  <-- NEW: own image, no longer reuses openalgo image
+│   ├── core/  signals/  slicers/  dashboard/  input/  data/
+│   └── pyproject.toml              <-- NEW: installable as `pip install -e .`
+│
+├── patches/                        <-- the ONLY bridge into openalgo
+│   ├── apply_patches.ps1           <-- re-applies wiring after every upgrade
+│   └── pov_terminal.py             <-- copy of the blueprint (source of truth)
+│
+├── scripts/
+│   ├── run_pov.py                  <-- launcher moved OUT of openalgo root
+│   ├── upgrade_openalgo.ps1        <-- one command = safe upgrade
+│   └── smoke_test.py               <-- post-upgrade health check
+│
+└── data/                           <-- strategy settings, ledgers, JSONs
+```
+
+**Rule:** OpenAlgo folder is treated as a *service you consume*, not a codebase you edit.
+Everything of yours lives beside it and talks over HTTP/WS.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Implementation plan — 6 steps
+
+### Step 1 — Create the master directory and relocate (no behavior change)
+- `git clone` a **fresh, pristine** OpenAlgo into `my-trading-system/openalgo/`.
+- `git clone` / move `pov_engine/` into its own repo at `my-trading-system/pov_engine/`
+  (own `.git` = it can never be cleaned by OpenAlgo operations, including `git clean -fd`).
+- Move `run_pov.py` → `scripts/run_pov.py` (it already self-locates the project root
+  by searching parents for `pov_engine/` — verify after the move).
+
+### Step 2 — Make `pov_engine` installable
+- Add `pyproject.toml` → `pip install -e .` (or `uv pip install -e .`).
+- Then `from openalgo import api` + `from pov_engine.runner import run_with_config`
+  work from anywhere — the `_sdkpath.py` hack becomes a fallback, not a requirement.
+- Benefits: dashboard, runner, and future engines import cleanly in any venv/container.
+
+### Step 3 — Replace in-tree wiring with a re-appliable patch
+- `patches/pov_terminal.py` — canonical copy of the blueprint.
+- `patches/apply_patches.ps1`:
+  1. copies `pov_terminal.py` into `openalgo/blueprints/`,
+  2. injects the two-line import + `register_blueprint` into `openalgo/app.py`
+     **idempotently** (skips if marker already present),
+  3. exits non-zero with a clear message if upstream `app.py` changed shape.
+- You then **commit nothing** to the openalgo repo — a `git pull` is always clean.
+- Alternative (cleaner, no patching at all): run the dashboard standalone and embed it
+  in the OpenAlgo UI via the existing `POV_DASH_URL` iframe mechanism — then the
+  blueprint may not even be needed. Decide during implementation.
+
+### Step 4 — Own compose file
+- Move the `pov-dash` (and any future `pov-engine`) service out of
+  `openalgo/docker-compose.yaml` into `my-trading-system/docker-compose.yml`.
+- Use `pov_engine/Dockerfile` (own image: python base + `pip install -e ./pov_engine`).
+- Networks: join the `openalgo` compose network, or talk over
+  `HOST_SERVER=http://localhost:5000` — either works; compose network preferred.
+- Mounts: `./pov_engine/input:/app/input`, `./data:/app/data` (read-only where possible).
+- Result: upgrading OpenAlgo = `git -C openalgo pull` + `docker compose up -d openalgo`
+  — your services don't even restart.
+
+### Step 5 — One-command upgrade SOP (`scripts/upgrade_openalgo.ps1`)
+```
+1. Backup:  copy .env, openalgo/db → backup/<date>/
+2. git -C openalgo stash pull / pull --ff-only  (abort on conflict)
+3. uv sync / pip install -r requirements.txt (in openalgo venv)
+4. patches/apply_patches.ps1               (re-wire blueprint)
+5. python scripts/smoke_test.py            (Step 6)
+6. docker compose up -d                    (both apps)
+7. Report PASS/FAIL per check; roll back via backup on failure
+```
+
+### Step 6 — Post-upgrade smoke test (`scripts/smoke_test.py`)
+Asserts, in order:
+1. OpenAlgo responds on `/auth/check-setup` (server alive).
+2. `client.analyzerstatus()` / `client.quotes()` succeed with your API key (SDK contract intact).
+3. `pov_engine` imports cleanly (`import pov_engine; import pov_engine.runner`).
+4. `python -m pov_engine.runner --help`-style dry parse of `input/master.json` (config schema valid).
+5. Dashboard responds on `:8050/_dash`.
+6. Blueprint endpoint `openalgo:5000/pov-terminal/config` returns `{url, embedded}`.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Risk & safety guardrails (institutional desk view)
+
+- **Never run an upgrade mid-session.** The SOP script should refuse to run during
+  market hours (09:15–15:30 IST) or if `positionbook` shows open positions.
+- **DB backup before every upgrade** (`openalgo/db` — migrations are one-way).
+- **Pin the SDK**: keep `openalgo==2.0.3` pinned in `pov_engine`'s pyproject; bump
+  deliberately, not silently with OpenAlgo upgrades.
+- **Analyzer-mode first**: after every upgrade, run one POV cycle in analyzer mode
+  (`ANALYZER=black`) before going live — the engine's mode is UI-controlled by design.
+- **Ledger continuity**: `pov_engine/core/ledger.py` state must be on a mounted
+  volume (`data/`), never inside the openalgo tree.
+
+## 5. Effort estimate
+
+| Phase | Time |
+|---|---|
+| Steps 1–2 (relocate + installable package) | ~1 day |
+| Step 3 (patch system) | ~0.5 day |
+| Steps 4–6 (compose, SOP, smoke test) | ~1 day |
+| **Total** | **~2–3 days** |
+
+## 6. Immediate zero-cost protection (do today, before any restructuring)
+
+```powershell
+# 1. Backup the whole engine + wiring now
+Copy-Item -Recurse pov_engine ..\pov_engine_backup_$(Get-Date -f yyyyMMdd)
+Copy-Item run_pov.py, blueprints\pov_terminal.py, docker-compose.yaml ..\pov_engine_backup_$(Get-Date -f yyyyMMdd)\
+
+# 2. Confirm pov_engine is untracked (it is — but verify)
+git status --short
+```
+
+If you don't do Phases 1–6 immediately, this backup alone guarantees nothing is lost.
+
+---
+
+*End of plan. On approval, implementation proceeds in the step order above, with the
+smoke test as the final acceptance gate.*
