+# OCL Live Trading Dashboard
+
+A terminal-rendered (rich) dashboard that:
+
+1. **Polls live quotes** for every watched NSE symbol.
+2. **Subscribes to the OCL screener** - new matches surface in real time.
+3. **Runs a per-symbol POV state machine** that decides when to accumulate, slow down, stop, or exit.
+4. **Tracks a virtual ledger** (cash, positions, realized + unrealized P&L).
+
+```
++------------------------------------------------------- OCL Trading Dashboard -----------------------------+
+|  CONNECTED   Symbols 25  Quote 3s  Scan 30s  Last quote 14:32:11  Cash 99,120  Realized +120  Unreal... |
++--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
+                                       Watchlist                                    +--------- Detail - INFY --------+
+| Symbol     |   LTP  | Chg%  | Bid   | Ask   | Spr%  |   Vol  | Pattern | Trigger | Dist% | Pos | P&L  | State      |
+|------------+--------+-------+-------+-------+-------+--------+---------+---------+-------+-----+------+-----------|
+| INFY NSE   | 1480.5 | -0.45 | 1480.0| 1481.0| 0.067 | 1.2M   | RRG     | 1475.0  | +0.37 |  50 | +250 | ACCUMULATING |
+| TCS NSE    | 3450.0 | +1.25 | 3449.5| 3450.5| 0.029 |  567K  | -       |    -    |    -  |   - |   -  | WATCHING    |
+| ...                                                                                                  |
+                                                                                                +------ Alerts (live) ------+
+                                                                                                | 14:31:55 MATCH  INFY RRG @ 1475.0 |
+                                                                                                | 14:32:11 TRADE  BUY 10 INFY @ 1480.50 |
+```
+
+## Quick start
+
+```bash
+# Default: NIFTY 50, paper mode, short_term risk-managed sizing.
+python -m pov_engine.dashboard.cli
+
+# Custom preset
+python -m pov_engine.dashboard.cli --preset NIFTY100
+
+# Custom config file
+python -m pov_engine.dashboard.cli --config pov_engine/input/dashboard.example.json
+
+# Restrict exchange (e.g. BSE-only)
+python -m pov_engine.dashboard.cli --preset NIFTY50 --exchange NSE
+
+# Investing mode (fixed qty_per_fire, no risk-based sizing)
+python -m pov_engine.dashboard.cli --mode investing --qty 50
+
+# LIVE TRADING (emits real broker orders on every BUY/SELL)
+# DANGEROUS - read the safety section below first.
+OPENALGO_API_KEY=... python -m pov_engine.dashboard.cli --live
+```
+
+## Two modes
+
+| Mode | Sizing |
+|------|--------|
+| `investing` (fixed) | `qty_per_fire` shares per tick. Use when you have a pre-decided position size and want the dashboard to obey it. |
+| `short_term` (default, risk-managed) | `qty_per_fire = floor(available_cash * risk_pct / ltp)`. Caps the loss on a SL hit to `risk_pct` of your cash per symbol. |
+
+## POV state machine
+
+Each symbol transitions through these states as the LTP walks through the OCL trigger level:
+
+```
+   WATCHING --[OCL match]--> MATCHED --[LTP in touch band]--> ACCUMULATING
+                                                          |
+                                          +---------------+---------------+
+                                          |               |               |
+                                LTP <= floor    LTP in [touch band]   LTP >= ceiling
+                                          |               |               |
+                                          v               v               v
+                                        SLOW       continues ACCUMULATING   STOPPED
+                                          |
+                                LTP <= stop_loss
+                                          |
+                                          v
+                                      EXITED -> COMPLETED
+```
+
+### Bands (configurable in the config file)
+
+| Band | Default | Meaning |
+|------|---------|---------|
+| Touch buffer | ±0.05% | LTP must be within this band of the trigger level to start accumulating. |
+| Ceiling | trigger +1.0% | LTP at or above this level stops accumulation (target reached). |
+| Floor | trigger -1.0% | LTP at or below this level slows POV to `pov_min_pct` (5% by default). |
+| Stop loss | trigger -2.0% | LTP at or below this level exits the full position. |
+
+## What the columns mean
+
+| Column | Meaning |
+|--------|---------|
+| LTP | Last-traded-price. |
+| Chg% | Percent change vs previous close. |
+| Bid/Ask | Best bid / best ask (live). |
+| Spr% | (ask - bid) / mid * 100. Use this to gauge liquidity. |
+| Vol | Day's volume. |
+| Pattern | RRG / GRR / - (no OCL match). |
+| Trigger | The OCL trigger level for the current match. |
+| Dist% | (LTP - trigger) / trigger * 100. Closer to zero = the touch is closer. |
+| Pos | Virtual position size in shares. |
+| P&L | Unrealized P&L on the virtual position. |
+| State | WATCHING / MATCHED / ACCUMULATING / SLOW / STOPPED / EXITED / COMPLETED. |
+
+## Where the OCL data comes from
+
+The dashboard tails the `OclScreenerMatch` table (written by
+`pov_engine/screener/ocl_screener_jobs.py`). For new matches to
+appear live, you must have at least one `OclScreenerConfig` with
+`is_active = true` and a sane `cron_expression`. Run a one-shot
+scan via `POST /api/v1/ocl-screener/scan` to seed the DB with
+matches even if you don't have a saved config yet.
+
+## SAFETY: live mode
+
+By default the dashboard runs in **paper mode** - every BUY/SELL
+intent is recorded in a virtual ledger and shown on the UI, but
+**no order is sent to the broker**. The cash, positions, and P&L
+you see are entirely simulated.
+
+To enable real trading:
+
+```bash
+OPENALGO_API_KEY=... \
+HOST_SERVER=http://127.0.0.1:5000 \
+WEBSOCKET_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:8765 \
+python -m pov_engine.dashboard.cli --live
+```
+
+`--live` flips the dashboard from paper to real orders. It will
+call `openalgo.client.placeorder` on every BUY/SELL intent the
+state machine emits. There is no confirmation prompt; a stop-loss
+hit will fire a SELL within seconds.
+
+Recommendation: run in paper mode for at least one trading day,
+review the trade log (`/api/v1/ocl-screener/configs/<id>/matches`
++ the local trade history), and only then switch to `--live`.
+
+## Config file reference
+
+See `pov_engine/input/dashboard.example.json` for a complete example. Keys:
+
+| Key | Default | Notes |
+|-----|---------|-------|
+| `watchlist_preset` | `"NIFTY50"` | One of `NIFTY50`, `BANKNIFTY`, `FINNIFTY`, `NIFTY100`. `null` for custom. |
+| `extra_symbols` | `[]` | List of `{symbol, exchange}` to add to the watchlist. |
+| `exchange_filter` | `null` | Restrict to one exchange (`"NSE"`, `"BSE"`, ...). |
+| `max_symbols` | `25` | Cap on the number of rows in the table. |
+| `quote_refresh_seconds` | `3.0` | Quote poll cadence. |
+| `scan_refresh_seconds` | `30.0` | Screener match poll cadence. |
+| `lookback_days` | `7` | How many days of history to pull for the detail panel. |
+| `starting_cash` | `100000` | Virtual cash. |
+| `mode` | `"short_term"` | `"investing"` or `"short_term"`. |
+| `qty_per_fire` | `100` | Shares per fire in investing mode. |
+| `risk_pct` | `0.01` | Per-symbol risk (1% of cash) in short_term mode. |
+| `touch_buffer_pct` | `0.05` | Width of the touch band around trigger. |
+| `ceiling_pct_above_trigger` | `1.0` | Stop accumulating above trigger + this %. |
+| `floor_pct_below_trigger` | `1.0` | Slow POV below trigger - this %. |
+| `stop_loss_pct_below_trigger` | `2.0` | Exit below trigger - this %. |
+| `pov_min_pct` | `5.0` | POV rate when in SLOW state. |
+| `pov_max_pct` | `25.0` | POV rate when ACCUMULATING. |
+
+## Limitations
+
+- **Short selling is not yet implemented** in the dashboard. GRR
+  (bearish) matches show in the alerts feed and the universe
+  table, but the state machine does not emit SELL-to-short intents.
+- **Fundamental data** (market cap, P/E) is not surfaced because
+  your broker does not return it through the existing endpoints.
+  The detail panel shows what's available: open/high/low/close,
+  volume, prev_close, the OCL pattern, and the position ledger.
+- **The dashboard is single-process** - it polls the DB for
+  matches rather than reading from a websocket. Latency is bounded
+  by `scan_refresh_seconds`.
\ No newline at end of file
