+# Percentage-of-volume equity order
+
+`POST /api/v1/povorder` starts an asynchronous cash-equity execution. The
+executor polls cumulative traded volume and submits no more than
+`participation_pct` percent of each interval's newly observed volume.
+
+```json
+{
+  "apikey": "<your_app_apikey>",
+  "symbol": "INFY",
+  "exchange": "NSE",
+  "action": "BUY",
+  "total_quantity": 1000,
+  "participation_pct": 10,
+  "duration": 900,
+  "interval": 15,
+  "product": "CNC",
+  "order_mode": "LIMIT",
+  "max_slice_quantity": 100,
+  "ceiling_price": 1500,
+  "stop_loss_price": 1470,
+  "exit_participation_pct": 30,
+  "limit_expiry_pct": 80,
+  "cutoff_time": "15:15",
+  "squareoff_time": "15:20",
+  "sme_periodic_call_auction": null,
+  "auction_windows": ["09:15-15:30"],
+  "persist_across_days": true,
+  "cancellation_cool_off_seconds": 2,
+  "max_order_to_trade_ratio": 10,
+  "idempotency_key": "infy-pov-20260902"
+}
+```
+
+`duration` and `interval` are seconds. `order_mode` is `MARKET` or `LIMIT`.
+In LIMIT mode, the latest best bid is used for BUY orders and the latest best
+ask for SELL orders. `max_slice_quantity` caps each child order.
+`ceiling_price` is required for BUY LIMIT orders (including the BUY exit of a
+SELL POV with a stop) and prevents placement when the best bid is above the
+ceiling. Only `NSE`/`BSE` equity and `CNC`/`MIS` products are accepted. When
+`stop_loss_price` is reached, the executor stops accumulating, reverses the action, and exits the quantity actually filled.
+The exit uses `exit_participation_pct` (default `30`) and continues until that
+quantity is filled. The response contains an `execution_id`; poll
+LIMIT children are cancelled before the next volume calculation after
+`limit_expiry_pct` percent of the interval (default `80`), preventing stale
+orders from remaining in the book.
+`cutoff_time` and `squareoff_time` are absolute IST exchange controls. At the
+cutoff, accumulation stops, open children are cancelled, and any filled
+quantity enters the configured exit POV. No exit orders are sent after the
+square-off time.
+
+The symbol master is consulted with `get_symbol_info` before an execution is
+accepted. SME/periodic-call-auction symbols only submit children inside
+`auction_windows` (a list such as `["09:15-10:15", "10:15-11:15"]`); outside a
+window the execution is durably hibernated. The default window is the regular
+equity session and can be overridden per request.
+
+For m.Stock, broker-provided `equilibriumPrice` and `matchedVolume` (including
+their supported auction aliases) are normalized to `auction_price` and
+`auction_volume`. If either value is absent, the auction cycle hibernates
+without guessing a price or volume.
+
+T2T, BE, and ST series are identified from symbol metadata. A same-day reverse
+exit is not submitted for these delivery-restricted series; the execution
+hibernates and retries on the next trading day. This prevents an automated POV
+exit from creating an invalid delivery settlement.
+
+Executions persist their deadline, child ledger, and fill/cancel counters. They
+hibernate while the exchange is closed and are recovered automatically at
+application startup. `persist_across_days` can be set to `false` to expire an
+execution at the first market close.
+
+LIMIT child replacement is protected by a cooling-off period of at least three
+intervals (45 seconds for a 15-second interval), or the configured
+`cancellation_cool_off_seconds` when it is longer. `min_order_interval_seconds`
+(default 1 second) and `max_order_to_trade_ratio` (default 10) provide
+additional protection against broker and exchange order-rate limits.
+After each cancellation request, the executor polls broker order status until
+the order is confirmed `cancelled`, `rejected`, or fully `filled`. A transition
+fails closed when confirmation is not received within
+`cancellation_confirmation_timeout_seconds` (default 10 seconds).
+
+Deployment defaults can be set with `POV_MAX_DURATION_SECONDS`,
+`POV_SME_AUCTION_WINDOWS`, `POV_CANCEL_COOL_OFF_SECONDS`,
+`POV_MIN_ORDER_INTERVAL_SECONDS`, and `POV_ORDER_TO_TRADE_RATIO` in `.env`.
+
+The executor reads the official `lotsize` from the symbol master before
+starting. The target quantity and `max_slice_quantity`, when supplied, must be
+exact multiples of that lot size. Every calculated child is rounded down to a
+whole lot; if the best depth contains less than one lot, that child is skipped.
+For example, an SME symbol with a lot size of `1000` accepts `1000`, `2000`, or
+`3000`, but rejects a target of `2500` and never submits a `250`-share child.
+
+Before volume is calculated, the executor checks quote trading status. `HALTED`
+and `PRE-OPEN` pause the execution as `PAUSED_BY_EXCHANGE`; a generic `AUCTION`
+also pauses unless the symbol is an SME periodic-call-auction instrument inside
+its configured window. It resumes only after a normal/allowed auction status is
+reported. It also pauses when a BUY is within 0.5% of the upper circuit or a SELL
+is within 0.5% of the lower circuit.
+`GET /api/v1/povorder/{execution_id}` with the same API key to view status,
+submitted quantity, remaining quantity, and child order IDs. A supplied
+`idempotency_key` makes retries return the existing execution; reusing it with
+different order parameters returns a conflict. Terminal statuses are
+`completed` when the target is submitted, `failed` when quote or child-order
+errors stop execution, and `expired` when the time window ends before the target
+is submitted.
+
+Before an execution starts, BUY orders are checked against the account's
+available cash using the limit/ceiling price, or the current quote when no
+price is supplied. SELL orders are checked against the current equity holdings
+for the requested symbol and exchange. These are pre-trade checks; cash and
+holdings can change while child orders are executing.
+
+For a BUY POV, a stop at `1470` stops further BUY orders and starts SELL POV
+orders at 30%. For example, if 600 shares were submitted before the trigger,
+the executor sells those 600 shares and does not buy the remaining target.
